WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:09.760
China and Iran signed a Comprehensive
Strategic Partnership in March 2021,

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.080
strengthening economic and security
cooperation between the two countries.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.050
According to media reports, the
investment amount is $400 billion USD

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.160
across 25 years, but the chinese government has

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.960
yet to confirm this number.
Here's why: China's Ministry of Commerce

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.949
has the cumulative stock of Chinese
investment in Iran at barely over $3 billion

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:38.399
at the end of 2019. The China Global Investment Tracker
has total chinese investment in Iran at

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:44.399
$4.7 billion from 2005 to 2020.
Chinese companies have promised Iran

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:48.924
large projects in the past. For example,
China National Petroleum Corporation's

00:00:48.924 --> 00:00:55.840
contract to develop phase 11 of the South Pars Gas Field
failed because of project delays and US sanctions.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.870
The tracker pegs the dollar value of
failed Chinese projects in Iran at $25.9 billion,

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:06.923
dwarfing realized spending. All of this casts doubt on large investment promises in the partnership.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.960
Do you think the China–Iran partnership
will be successful?

